            <div xml:id="d687">

                <pb facs="0764" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 25010/36.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Italian
                        Chargé.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-07-22"><hi rendition="#italic">July 22,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 869.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The department has received your note of
                    the 12th instant, inclosing a copy of the warrant of arrest, issued June 13
                    last, by the examining magistrate of the civil and criminal court of Como
                    against Mr. Porter Charlton.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to inform you that the entire matter is now in the
                    hands of the court, to whom all documents, papers, etc., which the Italian
                    Government may have to offer in the case should now be presented.</p>
                <p>The copy of the warrant is returned herewith.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
